openapi: 3.0.3
info:
  title: Tasky API
  description: |
    REST API for Tasky — Mongolia's most trusted domestic service marketplace.

    ## Authentication
    All endpoints (unless noted) require a Bearer JWT in the `Authorization` header.
    Phase 0-1 auth uses Facebook OAuth (`/auth/facebook`).
    Phase 2+ adds phone OTP auth (`/auth/otp/request`, `/auth/otp/verify`) and OTP becomes primary for new signups.

    ## Pagination
    All list endpoints use **cursor-based pagination**.
    Pass `cursor` (opaque string) and `limit` (default 20, max 100) as query parameters.
    Responses wrap results in `{ data: [], cursor: { next, has_more } }`.

    ## Errors
    All errors return a standard JSON body: `{ code, message, trace_id }`.

    ## Currency
    All monetary amounts are integers in MNT (Mongolian Tugrik).

    ## Idempotency
    Critical state-changing endpoints require an `Idempotency-Key` header.

    ## Phase Gating
    Two classes of deferred endpoints exist in this spec:
    - **Implemented and gated** (`wallet`, `payment`, `payout`): endpoints exist in the server and return `503` when
      their feature toggle is disabled. Current toggles: `escrow_enabled` (Phase 3+).
    - **Not yet implemented** (`lead-unlock`, `credits`, `referrals`, `subscription`, `business`,
      `instant-match`, `/verification/dan/verify`): endpoints are specified here as forward references for Phase 2/3+
      implementation. Until then they return `404`.
      Each such endpoint is annotated with `x-tasky-status: deferred` and `x-tasky-target-phase`.
    Current launch posture is Phase 1 zero monetization; seeded feature toggles may exist before their runtime
    consumers are implemented. See `docs/quality/capability-matrix.md` and `docs/quality/launch-baseline-2026-04.md`
    for current activation status.
  version: 1.3.0
  contact:
    name: Tasky Engineering
servers:
  - url: /api/v1
    description: API v1

